{
  "chapterId": "f3math-01",
  "reviewed": false,
  "intro": {
    "hook": {
      "en": "A single bacterium splits into two every 20 minutes. After 10 splits there are 2¹⁰ = 1024 bacteria. Indices let us write huge repeated multiplications in a few characters.",
      "bm": "Satu bakteria membahagi kepada dua setiap 20 minit. Selepas 10 kali pembahagian terdapat 2¹⁰ = 1024 bakteria. Indeks membolehkan pendaraban berulang yang besar ditulis dengan ringkas."
    },
    "bigIdeas": [
      {
        "en": "aⁿ means a multiplied by itself n times; a is the base and n is the index.",
        "bm": "aⁿ bermaksud a didarab dengan dirinya sendiri sebanyak n kali; a ialah asas dan n ialah indeks."
      },
      {
        "en": "Multiply → add indices; divide → subtract indices; power of a power → multiply indices.",
        "bm": "Darab → tambah indeks; bahagi → tolak indeks; kuasa bagi kuasa → darab indeks."
      },
      {
        "en": "a⁰ = 1, a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ and a^(1/n) = ⁿ√a (a ≠ 0).",
        "bm": "a⁰ = 1, a⁻ⁿ = 1/aⁿ dan a^(1/n) = ⁿ√a (a ≠ 0)."
      }
    ],
